 ChatApp

A console-based Java application built for the Programming 1A PoE (PROG5121).
Part 1 implements a user registration and login feature.

 Features

- Username validation - must contain an underscore and be no more than
  five characters long.
- Password complexity validation- must be at least eight characters
  long and contain a capital letter, a number, and a special character.
- South African cell phone number validation** — must contain the
  international country code (+27) followed by the number, validated
  using a regular expression.
- Login authentication - verifies entered credentials against the
  details captured at registration.

 Project Structure

- Login.java - contains all validation and authentication logic
  (checkUserName, checkPasswordComplexity, checkCellPhoneNumber,
  registerUser, loginUser, returnLoginStatus).
- ChatApp.java - console entry point that collects user input and
  drives the registration and login flow.
- LoginTest.java - JUnit tests covering both the individual validation
  methods and the full registration/login message flow, using the exact
  test data provided in the assignment brief.

 Testing

All validation logic is unit tested with JUnit 5. Tests cover both
assertTrue/assertFalse checks on the boolean validation methods, and
assertEquals checks on the exact message strings returned by
registerUser() and returnLoginStatus().

